# Worker secrets for local runs (`npm run dev:worker`). Copy to .dev.vars (ignored by git) and fill in.
# A provider without both values is off: no sign-in button, no /api/auth/<provider> route.
# On the hosting set the same names with `npx wrangler secret put <NAME>`.

# Google Cloud Console → Google Auth Platform → Clients → Web application.
# Authorized redirect URI for local runs: http://localhost:8787/api/auth/google/callback
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# GitHub → Settings → Developer settings → OAuth Apps → New OAuth App (an OAuth App, not a GitHub App).
# Authorization callback URL for local runs: http://localhost:8787/api/auth/github/callback
# Use a separate OAuth App for local runs, so the site's secret never sits on a dev machine; the site's app
# has https://ai-engineer-cookbook.olgln.workers.dev/api/auth/github/callback.
GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
